ró-man, n. hair on the body of men 🞄and animals (gnly. excluding the long hair 🞄of the head, beard, mane, or tail);
 plumage;
 🞄fish-scales (rare).

ro-mantha, m. ruminating, chewing 🞄the cud;
 chewing (of betel);
 frequent repetition.

roma-pulaka, m. bristling of the 🞄hair, thrill;
 -baddha, pp. woven out of hair;
