 -rājī̆, f. line or 🞄[] 🞄streak of hair (esp. above the navel in women, 🞄as a mark of puberty): (i) -patha, m. waist;
 🞄-vat, a. hairy;
 -vikriyā, f. horripilation, 🞄thrill.

roma-harṣa, m. bristling of the 🞄hair, thrill (caused by cold, fear, joy, anger, 🞄or wantonness);
 -harṣaṇa, a. causing the 🞄hair to bristle, thrilling (with rapture or 🞄horror);
 -harṣin, a. whose hair is bristing, 🞄thrilled.

